**GROUP ONE - TASK III (10 marks)**

The C program and the Pascal program below do the same job (the printed line numbers are not part of the programs; the questions quote the printed numbering: line 14 of the C program and line 15 of the Pascal program).

**C program**

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main(void) {
    int a, b, c, prod;
    float avg;
    printf("Enter the value of a: ");
    scanf("%d", &a);
    printf("Enter the value of b: ");
    scanf("%d", &b);
    printf("Enter the value of c: ");
    scanf("%d", &c);
    avg = (float) (a + b + c) / 3.0;
    prod = a * b * c;
    if (a > b)
        printf("Average: %.2f\n", avg);
    else
        printf("Product: %d\n", prod);
    getchar();
}
```

**Pascal program**

```pascal
program Numbers;
var
    a, b, c, prod : integer;
    avg : real;
begin
    write ('Enter the value of a: ');
    read (a);
    write ('Enter the value of b: ');
    readln (b);
    write ('Enter the value of c: ');
    readln (c);
    avg := (a+b+c)/3;
    prod := a * b * c;
    if (a > b) then
        writeln ('Average: ', avg:0:2)
    else
        writeln ('Product: ', prod);
    readln;
end.
```
